WEBVTT

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:08.650
It was a lot of fun, Kahoko.

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:16.200
You were the best way to kill time.

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:59.570
Our Cadenza.

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:02.920
OK! Did everyone get a handout?

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:06.010
The theme of the final selection has been decided.

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:10.980
The theme is: Liberation.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:25.540
This is the last performance of the competition, so give us a performance that you won't regret.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:28.770
That you won't regret...

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:32.960
I wonder if Yunoki is unpacking his bags about now?

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:36.210
Because of the time difference, he might already be asleep.

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:39.410
How much time difference is there between here and England?

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:40.570
I don't know...

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:44.090
Th-This is...

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:48.840
Is this the effect of Yunoki-sempai studying abroad?

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:56.960
Oh, everyone is together...

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:02.490
Speaking of which, it's almost time for the final selection.

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:05.370
But, without him...

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:10.030
There is no merit to a stage without its leading man.

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:14.540
If you think about it that way, Seiso Academy without Yunoki-sama is just...

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:25.180
Without merit, huh?

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:27.530
Just let her talk.

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:31.600
She'll quiet up once she hears our performances in the concert hall.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:32.880
Tsuchiura-kun!

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:38.780
That's right! We've got to make the final selection the best yet, for Yunoki's sake!

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:41.150
We've all got to do it together!

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:43.410
Hihara-sempai.

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:46.690
And anyway, I believe in him.

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:49.660
I believe that Yunoki will come back to music.

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:53.100
That's right.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:44.080
You aren't putting enough pressure on the strings.

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:46.660
Tsukimori-kun...

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:50.760
You should also fix that bad habit of sticking out your elbow too far.

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:52.780
Right.

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:58.420
How is your violin doing?

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:03.070
Yeah... It's my own ability that's the problem.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:05.040
You aren't scared?

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:12.120
I can feel that you are harder on yourself than anyone.

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:16.170
Aren't you scared to appear on stage as you are now?

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:20.110
I'd be lying to say I wasn't scared.

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:22.880
But as long as I'm together with this violin...

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:28.270
It's what introduced me to music.

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:30.750
And you, too, Tsukimori-kun... And everyone else...

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:35.310
I want to stand on the stage with this violin that has given me so much.

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:38.010
I see.

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:41.950
Hino...

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:47.100
I've give my best until the end, right...

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:55.110
Hino... And yet, you're...

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:10.370
Liberation, huh?

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:13.620
I've got to liberate myself as well.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:15.390
If I don't...

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:20.560
I decided to just work through it, step by step, without rushing.

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:23.310
I've got to make her smile.

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:29.000
For the final selection I'll play that piece!

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:50.630
Ah, you saved me!

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:52.750
Thank you, Hino-chan!

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:54.260
I give you my thanks!

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:56.230
Ah, it's nothing...

00:06:56.230 --> 00:07:00.040
It's nearly time for the next special issue!

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:02.750
OK, now before I forget...

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:07.740
Put this in the "to develop" bin.

00:07:08.230 --> 00:07:09.450
And that's that!

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:18.530
Ah, geez...

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:20.620
Now I've done it.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:21.830
Oops!

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:28.740
Amo-san, what's this?

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:32.010
This comes first. We can't have dust getting on it.

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:40.640
So you take care of the camera yourself?

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:45.290
Well, it's something I keep with me all the time.

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:49.990
This camera is a bit old, but it's been a good partner to me.

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:52.160
A partner, huh?

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:56.410
I hope me and my violin will become good partners, too.

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:06.790
What's this?

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:08.740
A cassette tape?

00:08:09.980 --> 00:08:12.490
It looks pretty old.

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:14.970
And I can't read the label on it.

00:08:15.310 --> 00:08:17.220
I wonder what kind of tape it is?

00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:20.810
Ooh, neat! Have we discovered a mysterious lost tape?

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:24.650
In that case... Oops, sorry!

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:34.490
Please, let this be a big scoop!

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:35.780
And, play!

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:00.580
Kanazawa-sensei.

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:11.190
Tell no one about this tape!

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:13.980
But, why?

00:09:29.390 --> 00:09:31.810
Kanazawa-sensei looked so...

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.120
Could that tape have been...

00:09:50.070 --> 00:09:53.080
Oh, Len, welcome home.

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:07.370
Um, about the charity concert you mentioned a while ago...

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:09.330
May I please participate?

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:18.960
I see, so you'll accept.

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:19.930
Thank you.

00:10:20.900 --> 00:10:25.360
No, it's just that I have someone I want to hear it.

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:26.250
Len?

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:29.560
Thank you very much.

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:46.140
I wonder who it was that opened his heart?

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:59.100
I also must overcome.

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:55.380
So you're back.

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:57.780
Ryo, that piece just now...

00:11:58.060 --> 00:12:00.440
It's the piece I'm playing for the final selection.

00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:04.740
It's the final chance, so I want to play the ultimate piece.

00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:09.960
So Ryo is playing that piece once again.

00:12:12.570 --> 00:12:17.840
Oh yes, that boy who came in with Hino-san...

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:19.800
Is he a friend of yours?

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:21.650
Just an acquaintance.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:24.240
Why do you ask?

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:28.140
I was just thinking that I'd seen him somewhere before...

00:12:31.780 --> 00:12:33.790
Ah, welcome.

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:35.050
Hino.

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:38.950
Tsuchiura-kun, are you practicing here today?

00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:40.790
Yeah. And you?

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:42.900
I was thinking I'd buy a pitch pipe.

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:45.430
If you're looking for a pitch pipe they are over there.

00:12:47.790 --> 00:12:49.360
Thank you very much.

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:52.670
Tuning from a pitch pipe?

00:12:52.670 --> 00:12:54.080
Shouldn't you have one already?

00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:57.170
Yeah, I suppose I should.

00:12:57.930 --> 00:13:03.250
Tuning, maintenance... I've got to remember it all, little by little.

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:07.260
Because this violin is my partner.

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:14.450
I'll be your pitch pipe today.

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:16.940
Thank you.

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:27.140
Did I hear something just now?

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:35.630
How is that?

00:13:35.630 --> 00:13:37.460
Yeah, sounds good, right?

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:40.020
OK, next comes the D string.

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:40.710
Right.

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:48.930
Oh, there was a musical instrument store over here.

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:56.030
I have a feeling like I've been here before.

00:13:57.650 --> 00:13:58.990
Tsukimori-kun!

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:01.150
This is...

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:05.860
That's rare for you to be spacing out like that, Tsukimori-kun.

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:08.490
Well...

00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:10.320
Isn't this...

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:13.280
Tsukimori-kun, do you know this shop?

00:14:13.280 --> 00:14:15.690
Yes, I've been here once before.

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:21.040
I also have a feeling I've been here before, but I just can't remember.

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:26.750
Hihara-sempai.

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:28.340
Tsukimori-kun.

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:29.960
Kaho-chan?

00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:31.380
Tsuchiura.

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:33.180
Ah! I remembered!

00:14:35.620 --> 00:14:37.350
It was in the first year of middle school...

00:14:38.330 --> 00:14:42.600
I was worried about deciding between track and field or the brass band.

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:48.470
Be careful on your way home, Ryo!

00:14:48.470 --> 00:14:49.910
I know!

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:52.830
Sorry.

00:14:53.520 --> 00:14:54.620
S-Sorry!

00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:08.600
Ooh, it's silver!

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:10.380
So cool!

00:15:12.880 --> 00:15:15.680
What are you hesitating for?

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:20.070
The answer is right in front of you, right?

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:27.070
And that's when I quit track and field and joined the brass band.

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:30.740
Oh, really? So that's what happened.

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:32.740
Ryo, I remembered!

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:34.270
I remembered!

00:15:35.590 --> 00:15:37.250
That's right, it was you!

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:47.120
It's Tsukimori-kun!

00:15:49.390 --> 00:15:51.470
Why do you have this?

00:15:51.670 --> 00:15:55.190
I knew I had seen you before somewhere.

00:15:55.740 --> 00:15:57.230
Enough already.

00:15:57.230 --> 00:16:00.690
Huh? But we just found it. Let's sit back and watch.

00:16:00.990 --> 00:16:02.890
I'm not at that level.

00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:06.150
That's right.

00:16:06.880 --> 00:16:08.980
That was my impetus.

00:16:10.920 --> 00:16:12.320
A competition?

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:15.690
Yes. You aren't interested, Ryo?

00:16:16.440 --> 00:16:20.370
I've been told to try entering I don't know how many times already...

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:24.820
But they're all such small stuff.

00:16:24.820 --> 00:16:26.350
Hey, now...

00:16:26.350 --> 00:16:29.130
I'm not getting a big head about it or anything.

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:33.110
That's it! Shall we watch the video from last year's competition?

00:16:35.340 --> 00:16:39.980
There was a kid who was about your age who was amazing.

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:01.660
H-He's...

00:17:02.340 --> 00:17:04.380
Amazingly good.

00:17:08.990 --> 00:17:15.440
It's because there were people as good as him that I thought entering the competition would be fun.

00:17:15.440 --> 00:17:16.640
But then...

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:22.730
I can't believe that was Tsukimori...

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:28.860
Mister, this is great! What a treasure trove!

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:31.190
Actually I have some of Ryo as well.

00:17:31.450 --> 00:17:32.720
What?

00:17:32.720 --> 00:17:34.520
I told you to erase them!

00:17:34.520 --> 00:17:36.620
No way I'd erase them!

00:17:36.620 --> 00:17:38.740
It's my precious collection, after all.

00:17:38.740 --> 00:17:41.000
I would most definitely like to view it.

00:17:41.440 --> 00:17:44.760
Mister, while I've got Tsuchiura held back, hurry up!

00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:46.500
Please, don't!

00:17:51.560 --> 00:17:53.720
The wind feels so nice!

00:17:54.410 --> 00:17:59.480
You're aiming to win the competition, am I right?

00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:00.760
Of course.

00:18:01.290 --> 00:18:02.990
I'm not going to lose.

00:18:02.990 --> 00:18:04.560
Not for the final selection.

00:18:05.740 --> 00:18:07.810
Yes, I accept your challenge.

00:18:08.320 --> 00:18:10.270
Osaki-sempai!

00:18:11.140 --> 00:18:12.450
Sempai!

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:17.950
A volunteer concert?

00:18:18.940 --> 00:18:21.040
You mentioned this to me before, didn't you?

00:18:21.040 --> 00:18:21.870
Yes.

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:24.870
Amazing! Everyone is going to perform!

00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:33.150
Come on now, everyone, cheer up.

00:18:33.150 --> 00:18:35.310
Let's try one more time.

00:18:35.310 --> 00:18:38.470
But no one wants to take them.

00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:46.990
Tsuchiura!

00:18:49.820 --> 00:18:51.560
Tsuchiura, how about it?

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:54.030
Sounds good to me.

00:18:57.500 --> 00:18:59.220
Hihara-sempai...

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:00.660
Tsuchiura-kun...

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:24.420
I've heard that piece before.

00:19:24.840 --> 00:19:27.370
It's Chopin's "The Entertainer."

00:19:34.850 --> 00:19:37.350
It's got this easygoing, free feeling.

00:19:37.350 --> 00:19:40.270
I think I like this kind of performance.

00:19:40.610 --> 00:19:42.060
OK, everyone.

00:19:42.060 --> 00:19:43.060
Yeah!

00:19:45.970 --> 00:19:46.930
Here.

00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:48.660
Please come.

00:19:58.560 --> 00:20:00.870
Music really is mysterious.

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:04.890
Those children were feeling down just before, but now they're having so much fun.

00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:11.410
Len, your music should be fun for you, as well as letting other people enjoy it.

00:20:31.880 --> 00:20:34.170
That was kind of fun.

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:35.250
Guess so.

00:20:36.730 --> 00:20:40.650
Are you playing Ave Maria for the final selection?

00:20:40.650 --> 00:20:45.120
Yeah. Are you playing the piece you were practicing at Southern Music, Tsuchiura-kun?

00:20:45.120 --> 00:20:46.730
You were listening?

00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:49.220
Yeah, just a bit outside.

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:52.810
It's Liszt's "La Campanella."

00:20:53.290 --> 00:20:57.480
It's the piece I played at the competition back in elementary school.

00:20:58.450 --> 00:21:01.510
I haven't played it once since then.

00:21:01.510 --> 00:21:05.380
But I've decided to liberate it.

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:12.450
When I look at how hard you are working, I can't stand myself for being dragged down by the past.

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:13.930
I'm not so...

00:21:13.930 --> 00:21:19.670
That piece was originally a violin concerto composed by Paganini.

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:21.130
Paganini?

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:26.430
Liszt was so moved when he heard Paganini give a recital,

00:21:26.430 --> 00:21:30.160
that he decided he would become the "Paganini of the Piano."

00:21:30.160 --> 00:21:31.580
Oh?

00:21:37.220 --> 00:21:38.480
Tsuchiura-kun?

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:43.980
I didn't think I'd ever be able to play that piece again.

00:21:45.290 --> 00:21:47.740
Just like Paganini was there for Liszt...

00:21:48.430 --> 00:21:52.450
I guess you could say that you are there as my violinist.

00:21:53.230 --> 00:21:55.340
Ts-Tsuchiura-kun...

00:23:36.370 --> 00:23:39.770
Lili's One Point Classic!

00:23:40.060 --> 00:23:44.350
The composer Liszt, called the greatest pianist of the 19th century,

00:23:44.350 --> 00:23:48.730
composed works for piano that required incredible technique and ability,

00:23:48.730 --> 00:23:52.940
but as he was also quite good looking he was also a superstar pianist,

00:23:52.940 --> 00:23:58.290
and there were episodes where the female fans listening to his concerts would faint.

00:23:58.290 --> 00:23:59.780
OK, now time for a quiz.

00:23:59.780 --> 00:24:05.090
Since Liszt's performances were such an amazing display of technique and ability, what nickname did he receive?

00:24:05.780 --> 00:24:07.760
What's the matter, Tsukimori-kun?

00:24:07.760 --> 00:24:10.910
Hino, take this.

00:24:10.910 --> 00:24:13.210
That envelope... Could it be...

00:24:13.210 --> 00:24:14.220
A letter of challenge?!

00:24:14.930 --> 00:24:17.500
Next episode: A Heartful Harmony.

00:24:17.500 --> 00:24:19.610
Now, let us do battle!

00:24:20.800 --> 00:24:24.250
The answer is... the "Piano Magician!"
